From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eleata <1222931+eleata@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:34:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41 server: token-in/token-out route behind
 TENSORFOLD_TOKEN_ROUTE

Adds POST /inference/v1/generate (vLLM token mode) with its validation, whole
and SSE replies, and the chat mailbox path that does not decode text. The route
is off by default; with TENSORFOLD_TOKEN_ROUTE=1 it is served and the API key
gate covers /inference/. /health reports the flag and /metrics counts its
results. TF_DS_API_EFFORTS=1 (engine, both ranks) selects the API's effort
table instead of the lane's.

Rebased onto the recipe's TF_REF fbbc971 with zig/patches 0001-0038 of
MiaAI-Lab main 0e7d421 applied, as zig/Dockerfile applies them; it was 0035
on 629c524 (#59). Changes for fbbc971 (as in #77's rebase): finish's content
code moved to the new finish with upstream's tool-only whitespace rule; the
.ids path calls upstream's spans; the first token's logprob is drawn in
Lanes.prefillPart. With 0032 the keep-alive ping and the route's types sit
side by side, and the ping loop calls commit(tokens, scored); with 0036 the
token route passes its cached prompt tokens to noteRequest, as the text path
does. NoGone.check is pub, as prepare_gate (0023) requires.

Audit fixes in chat.zig: a failed allocation in the mailbox or the reader no
longer drops a round silently (a token-only reply ends with OutOfMemory; the
text path is unchanged); a client that leaves during the held-back last round
cancels it as in any other round; the token reply's runtime object carries the
request's thinking and effort instead of false/null. A streamed token reply
gets the text routes' keep-alive: TokenSink has a ping, the SSE writer sends
": ping" after ping_after_ns of silence (a long cold prefill, when the route is
used without the gateway), and the silence is counted from the submit.
The route's refusals name the field instead of printing "{s}"; continuous
usage carries the prompt's cached tokens once the engine reports them; a
failed allocation (parsing, preparing, generating or building the reply) is a
500 (a constant body, so it needs no allocation), or an error event in a
stream, instead of a closed connection; a whole reply that cannot be
serialized, or whose logprobs cannot be built, is one of them.
On the rebase audit: the native path computes the system prefix and its
cache cuts for prompts with pictures again (the route had moved them into
prompt.prepare after the pictures' early return; the server measured them for
every prompt before); prompt ids' shared_prefixes move past the image spans
before them, as history_len does; /health reports features.logprobs from the
engine's info instead of false (the CUDA host does not report them yet, so
the route refuses them there and a gateway falls back); a reply's finish time
is taken where its end is known, before its text is decoded, as before the
route; the image-placeholder test checks both mismatches; the smoke test's
logprobs check follows TF_FAKE_LOGPROBS (35/35 with and without).
zig fmt applied.

Checked with Zig 0.17.0 on x86_64: zig build test 23/23 steps (529 tests on
the series alone; with the route the steps whose binaries changed ran again,
471, the rest cached); zig/tests/server: build.sh builds fake_serve and
tensorfold-native; zig_test.sh 130/130 and 96/96; token_route_smoke.py against
fake_serve 35/35 with TF_FAKE_LOGPROBS=0 and with 1.
